rofile (the 30 m DSM includes tree canopy).","Road bumps and ruts in the drive are illustrative; the grade and the line of the road are real.","Trees, shrubs, grass tufts and boulders are placed where WorldCover maps that cover; their size and number are illustrative.","The walking loop is a 30 m circle around the arrival point; it is not a mapped trail.","The shrine is drawn in the module: a square chamber on a stepped podium, a stair up the front, a domed roof on a drum, and a finial. It stands on the OSM tourism=attraction node named Stupa, 52 m north of the road.","Published by Wikipedia (Gumbat Stupa article): the main stupa's plinth is 17 m a side and has 'a projection of about 3.7m'. The photos do not show a plinth that wide beside the chamber, so the plinth is estimated at about 8 m a side and the 3.7 m projection is used as the stair's run. The 17 m figure is not reconciled with the photos.","Estimated, not measured: the chamber about 5.8 m square and 4.6 m high, the podium 1.5 m high, the stair 3.2 m wide with four treads, the dome about 5 m across and 2.9 m high, and the finial. The arched niches are dark recesses, not arches.","Not modelled: the two terraces, the monastery and the more than 20 smaller stupas named in the article; the ground is the real DEM, with a levelled terrace of 15 m radius.","Season colours, snow, ice and dawn mist are illustrative.","Traffic on the drive is illustrative: the vehicle kinds are those seen on Swat roads (Willys jeeps, Hilux, Suzuki vans, Mehran cars, CD70 motorbikes, Qingqi rickshaws, painted trucks); their number and movement are not counted."],"sources":[{"name":"Copernicus DEM GLO-30","use":"terrain heights","licence":"© DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA","url":"https://spacedata.copernicus.eu/collections/copernicus-digital-elevation-model"},{"name":"ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200","use":"trees, meadow, rock, snow","licence":"CC BY 4.0, © ESA WorldCover project 2021","url":"https://esa-worldcover.org"},{"name":"Wikipedia: Gumbat Stupa","use":"the 17 m plinth and 3.7 m projection (not reconciled with the photos); the site description","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gumbat_Stupa"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap node 5759001422 (tourism=attraction, name Stupa)","use":"the position of the shrine","licence":"ODbL 1.0","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5759001422"},{"name":"OpenStreetMap","use":"the primary road west from Barikot (ways 447684913 and 1298957628) and the Stupa node at the point","licence":"ODbL, © OpenStreetMap contributors","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}]}